# Cursor Rules for MultiModel AI Project

## Project Overview
This is a Python 3.13 project for building multimodal AI applications using LangChain, LangGraph, and various AI models.

## Code Style & Standards
- Use Python 3.13+ features and type hints
- Follow PEP 8 style guidelines
- Keep code clean and modular
- Use minimal, crisp comments (avoid obvious comments)
- Prefer function-based approach over classes when possible
- Use pathlib for file operations
- Use f-strings for string formatting
- Use verbose method naming for clarity
- Keep method descriptions short and concise
- Keep the project structure modular. There should be proper separation of concerns.

## Project Structure
- `src/main/` - Main package code (treat as primary package)
- `data/` - Downloaded datasets and data files
- `requirements.txt` - Python dependencies
- `pyproject.toml` - Project configuration

## Virtual Environment
- Always use `multimodal_ai_venv` for all Python commands

## Dependencies
- langchain, langchain-core, langchain-community, langchain-openai
- langgraph for stateful applications
- pydantic for data validation
- kaggle for dataset downloads
- python-dotenv for environment management

## Environment Variables
- Use environment variables wherever necessary for configuration
- Store sensitive data in `.env` file
- Use `python-dotenv` to load environment variables
- Never hardcode API keys or credentials

## Code Patterns
- Keep code clean and modular
- Use async/await for I/O operations when appropriate
- Implement proper error handling with try/except
- Use dataclasses or Pydantic models for data structures
- Prefer composition over inheritance

## Documentation
- Use short, concise docstrings for all public functions and classes
- Keep README.md updated with usage examples
- Document API endpoints and data formats

## Security
- Never commit API keys or sensitive data
- Use environment variables for configuration
- Validate all user inputs
- Use proper file permissions (600 for credential files)

## AI/ML Specific
- Use LangChain for LLM orchestration
- Implement proper prompt engineering
- Use LangGraph for complex workflows
- Handle multimodal data (text, images, audio) appropriately
- Implement proper model versioning and caching 